  "playbook": "## Vendor Overview\n\nShree Balaji Steel Traders Pvt Ltd (V001) is a frequent vendor for the team. The primary recurring exception involves freight charges attached to their invoices.\n\nShree Balaji Steel Traders Pvt Ltd (V001) is subject to standard accounts-payable controls, including mandatory e-invoicing for suppliers with a turnover exceeding Rs 5 crore, GSTIN verification, and Finance Controller approval for any invoice exceeding ₹5,00,000.\n\n## Freight Charge Exceptions\n\nThe team maintains a standing agreement for freight charges related to this vendor. Freight charges are permitted to be approved when they are ₹5,000.00 or less per trip, even if those charges are not explicitly listed on the corresponding purchase order or if minor discrepancies exist in the billing documentation. Any freight charges exceeding this amount must be placed on hold.\n\n## Standard Exception Handling Protocols\n\n- Duplicates: Any invoice sharing the same vendor and invoice number, or matching the amount and date of a previously processed invoice, must be rejected.\n- New Vendors: Invoices from newly onboarded vendors are escalated until KYC and bank verification are finalized.\n- Bank Changes: Any request to pay to a bank account differing from the vendor master must be escalated for treasury to perform a phone callback on the registered number.\n- Supplier GSTIN: Any discrepancy between the GSTIN on the invoice and the vendor master, or a failure in the GSTIN checksum, is treated as potential impersonation and requires immediate escalation.\n- E-invoicing: For suppliers exceeding the Rs 5 crore turnover threshold, the invoice must include a valid IRN and signed QR code; otherwise, the invoice must be held and a compliant document requested.",
